# Line endings, and the three places where normalising them would be a bug.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `scripts/split-status.py` wrote CRLF on Windows and
# the fix was commit cd5aa35 — a byte-level difference in a file whose
# bytes are checked. Without this file the same class of damage arrives
# from git itself, on the first clone, before anyone has run anything.
#
# Copyright (c) mesa-nvk-horizon contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# Everything text is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree.
# Not `core.autocrlf`-dependent: the build runs inside a Linux container
# even when the developer is on Windows, and a CRLF shebang line is a
# `bad interpreter` error there.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.build text eol=lf
*.cross text eol=lf

# --- The exceptions, and each one is a gate. -------------------------
#
# 1. The patch series. `scripts/apply-mesa-patches.sh` identifies a
#    patch by its subject *and* its `git patch-id`, so that an edited
#    diff under an unchanged subject is caught rather than reported as
#    already applied. Rewriting line endings changes the diff and
#    therefore the identity of every patch in the series.
*.patch -text

# 2. The hardware logs. They are evidence: verbatim console output whose
#    sha256 is recorded in docs/hw-logs/MANIFEST.sha256 and checked by
#    scripts/check-history-intact.sh. All 165 are LF today, which is the
#    point — a checkout that converted them, in either direction, would
#    fail that check on a tree nobody had edited, and the failure would
#    say the evidence had been altered.
docs/hw-logs/** -text

# 3. The working record moved out of STATUS.md, under the same manifest
#    and the same check (decision D17).
docs/history/** -text

# --- Binaries --------------------------------------------------------
*.nro binary
*.nso binary
*.nacp binary
*.a   binary
*.o   binary
*.spv binary

# GitHub's language statistics: docs/hw-logs/ is 166 console logs and
# docs/history/ is the working record. Neither is source, and together
# they are most of the repository by file count.
docs/hw-logs/** linguist-documentation
docs/history/** linguist-documentation
mesa-patches/*.patch linguist-vendored
